The leading explanation is the **superposition hypothesis** (Elhage et al., *Toy Models of Superposition*, 2022). A **feature** is a property of the input the model tracks, such as 'this text is base64' or 'this token is inside a DNA string'. The hypothesis says:

- each feature is a **direction** in activation space, not a single neuron;
- the model tracks **more features than it has dimensions**, so the directions cannot all be orthogonal;
- this works because most features are **sparse**: any given token activates only a few of them.
